{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Does he….</b> The sense: for the plowman works the ground time after time, and sows, and the earth by its nature produces the grain." "<b>Does he open and harrow.</b> He works the field, like ישדד לו יעקב (Hosea 10:11), and the meaning is doubled."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:40.953687959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}